        {
          "dimension": "Physical & operational security",
          "level": "High",
          "note": "The January 2025 kidnapping of co-founder David Balland for a reported €10M ransom, combined with a 2020 customer data breach exposing 270,000 physical addresses, demonstrates that hardware wallet ownership creates real-world targeting risk for both executives and users.",
          "source": "https://haveibeenpwned.com/Breach/Ledger"
        },
        {
          "dimension": "Centralization / custody model",
          "level": "Medium",
          "note": "Ledger Recover's proposal to shard and escrow seed phrases with third-party custodians contradicts the self-custody premise and triggered enough backlash that the launch was postponed, exposing governance tension between product growth and the user base's ideological commitments.",
          "source": "https://shop.ledger.com/pages/seed-phrase-storage"
        },
        {
          "dimension": "Smart-contract / protocol",
          "level": "Medium",
          "note": "XRP Ledger's brief validation halt in 2023-2024 and the broader risk of DeFi integrations through Ledger Live (EigenLayer restaking, stablecoin yields) expose hardware wallet users to on-chain protocol failures that the device itself cannot mitigate.",
